\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Benchmark visual diagnostics. Top: controlled multibasin systems where the pale background is the evaluation basin map, gray streamlines are the true vector field, colored dots mark support-family/basin matches, and black dots mark support-family/basin mismatches. The learned LISTA \(F_{\rm  top8}\) families are mapped post hoc to each family's dominant evaluation basin. Basin labels and counts are evaluation-only, and the catalog panels use the attractor-center basin convention from the validation figures. Bottom: Dysts $dt{\times }30$ $H5000$ phase portraits with held-out truth in gray and forecasts from the best seed-$0$ primary model. Dysts is used only for forecasting and has no basin labels.}}{3}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
